.TH PI-RS 1 "August 2026" "pi-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pi-rs \- High-performance, pure Rust autonomous coding agent and swarm orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pi-rs
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-print\fR \fI"QUERY"\fR [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL_ID\fR]
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-rpc\fR
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fIPATH_TO_SESSION.jsonl\fR [\fB\-\-replay-delay-ms\fR \fIMS\fR]
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-login\fR [\fIPROVIDER\fR]
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-models\fR | \fB\-\-refresh-models\fR
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
.br
.B pi-rs
\fB\-\-init\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pi-rs
is a 100% pure Rust reimplementation of Mario Zechner's Pi Coding Agent (\fBpi.dev\fR / \fBearendil-works/pi\fR).
Engineered for speed, safety, and zero external runtime dependencies (zero Node.js/V8/npm), \fBpi-rs\fR provides an interactive terminal user interface (TUI) powered by Ratatui, an asynchronous dual-protocol tool execution engine, a bi-directional JSON-RPC 2.0 server daemon for IDE integrations (Neovim/VSCode), and multi-agent swarm orchestration with First Mate and Herdr protocols.

\fBpi-rs\fR operates against a directed acyclic graph (DAG) session tree, allowing arbitrary branch rewinds, simulated rollback previews, branch visual diffs, and context window compaction when token usage approaches model context limits.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print " \fIQUERY\fR"
Run in one-shot CLI print mode. Executes the user's query against the configured model, emits agent events, prints the final response to standard output, and exits cleanly.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fIMODEL_ID\fR"
Specify the AI model identifier to use (e.g. \fIopencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\fR, \fIanthropic/claude-3-7-sonnet-latest\fR, \fIopenai/gpt-4o\fR, \fIkilo/deepseek-r1\fR, \fIollama/llama3\fR). Defaults to \fIopencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-rpc
Launch \fBpi-rs\fR in bidirectional JSON-RPC 2.0 daemon mode over standard input and standard output. Stdout is reserved exclusively for JSON-RPC messages and notifications; all operational logging is routed to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-models
Query local cache and display a formatted table of all discovered and configured AI models across 33+ LLM providers, including context window sizes and reasoning/vision capabilities.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh-models
Force refresh online provider endpoints and local daemons (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, Kilo), update the catalog cache in \fI~/.pi/agent/models.json\fR, and display available models.
.TP
.BR \-\-login " [\fIPROVIDER\fR]"
Launch the interactive authentication setup wizard. If \fIPROVIDER\fR is omitted, defaults to Anthropic. Prompts for the API key, validates format, and saves credentials to \fI~/.pi/config.json\fR and \fI~/.pi/agent/auth.json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-replay " \fIPATH_TO_SESSION.jsonl\fR"
Replay a recorded JSONL session trajectory to standard output with colorized role badges, executed tool calls, and step-by-step output streaming.
.TP
.BR \-\-replay-delay-ms " \fIMS\fR"
Specify the delay in milliseconds between steps during session replay. Defaults to 50ms.
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " \fISHELL\fR"
Generate shell autocompletion script to standard output for the specified shell. Supported values: \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, \fIfish\fR, \fIpowershell\fR, \fIelvish\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Initialize workspace configuration. Creates \fI~/.pi\fR and \fI~/.pi/agent\fR config files if absent, and scaffolds a starter \fIAGENTS.md\fR file in the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and usage synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.

.SH TUI INTERACTIVE CONTROLS & KEYBINDINGS
When executed without \fB\-\-print\fR or \fB\-\-rpc\fR, \fBpi-rs\fR starts an interactive terminal user interface.

.SS Keyboard Shortcuts
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Open the fuzzy Model Selector popup to search and hot-swap the active LLM provider and model.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open the Provider Picker overlay to switch active backends (Anthropic, OpenAI, OpenCode, Kilo, Ollama, OpenRouter, etc.).
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Open the Session DAG Tree visualizer to inspect conversation history nodes, parent-child branches, and navigate rewind points.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Rewind the active conversation branch to the previous user turn or selected DAG node.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Fork the conversation and initialize a clean, fresh session branch.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Interrupt active model streaming or cancel a long-running subprocess/tool execution. Pressing again when idle exits \fBpi-rs\fR.
.TP
.B Escape
Close any active popup modal, dialog, or autocompletion menu.
.TP
.B ?
Open the interactive Help & Keybindings cheat sheet.
.TP
.B PageUp / PageDown
Scroll conversation history view up or down.
.TP
.B Tab
Trigger slash-command and argument autocompletion in the input bar.

.SS Interactive Slash Commands
Type a leading slash \fB/\fR in the input bar to activate autocomplete:
.TP
.B /model [\fIquery\fR]
Search and switch active AI model directly from the command line.
.TP
.B /provider [\fIname\fR]
Switch active LLM provider.
.TP
.B /diff [\fInode_a\fR] [\fInode_b\fR]
Open the split-pane side-by-side Diff Viewer to compare file changes or branch states.
.TP
.B /tree
Display the full ASCII/Unicode session DAG history tree.
.TP
.B /session [\fInew|save|load|id\fR]
Manage session DAG persistence, export trajectories, or switch session files.
.TP
.B /theme [\fIname\fR]
Cycle or select UI theme (\fIdefault\fR, \fIdark\fR, \fIdracula\fR, \fInord\fR, \fIgruvbox\fR, \fImonokai\fR, \fIcatppuccin\fR).
.TP
.B /login [\fIprovider\fR]
Configure API key for a provider inside the TUI.
.TP
.B /clear
Clear visible viewport messages while preserving underlying session DAG history.
.TP
.B /compact
Force immediate context window compaction and summarize conversation history.
.TP
.B /help
Display the built-in reference documentation and command list.
.TP
.B /exit ", " /quit
Save session state and cleanly terminate \fBpi-rs\fR.

.SH JSON-RPC 2.0 API DAEMON
When started with \fB\-\-rpc\fR, \fBpi-rs\fR operates as a high-performance JSON-RPC 2.0 daemon over standard I/O for editor plugins (Neovim, VSCode, Emacs) and swarm agents.

.SS Request / Response Methods
.TP
.B pi/ping
Health check method. Returns server status and version string.
.TP
.B pi/prompt \fR{\fB"prompt"\fR: "..."}\fR
Run an agent turn with the given prompt. Streams intermediate tokens and tool notifications before returning final response.
.TP
.B pi/models \fR[{\fB"force"\fR: boolean}]\fR
List all available AI models. Set \fB"force": true\fR to refresh online provider endpoints.
.TP
.B pi/model/get
Get active model ID, provider, and endpoint configuration.
.TP
.B pi/model/set \fR{\fB"model"\fR: "..."}\fR
Hot-swap active LLM model ID during runtime.
.TP
.B pi/tools/list
Return JSON schema definitions for all registered native tools.
.TP
.B pi/tools/execute \fR{\fB"name"\fR: "...", \fB"arguments"\fR: {...}}\fR
Directly execute a native tool with specified JSON arguments and return output.
.TP
.B pi/skills/list
List all auto-discovered skill definitions loaded from \fIskills/\fR, \fI.pi/skills/\fR, and \fI~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/builtin/skills/\fR.
.TP
.B pi/mcp/list
List all active Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers and cached dynamic tools.
.TP
.B pi/session/history
Return chronological message history along the active DAG branch.
.TP
.B pi/session/rewind \fR{\fB"node_id"\fR: "..."}\fR
Rewind the active DAG pointer to a historical node.
.TP
.B pi/session/simulate_rewind \fR{\fB"target_node_id"\fR: "..."}\fR
Preview message history from rewinding without mutating active session state.
.TP
.B pi/session/fork
Fork active DAG node into a new branch point.
.TP
.B pi/session/new
Initialize a completely fresh session DAG tree.
.TP
.B pi/session/trajectory \fR[{\fB"branch_node_id"\fR: "..."}]\fR
Export full trajectory metadata and step timeline for evaluation or replay.
.TP
.B pi/session/diff \fR{\fB"node_a"\fR: "...", \fB"node_b"\fR: "..."}\fR
Compute structural diff and divergence between two branch points.

.SS Streaming Notifications (Server to Client)
.TP
.B pi/streamingChunk \fR{\fB"chunk"\fR: "..."}\fR
Emitted when model streams incremental text tokens.
.TP
.B pi/toolExecuting \fR{\fB"tool_name"\fR: "...", \fB"tool_call_id"\fR: "..."}\fR
Emitted when agent starts executing a native tool.
.TP
.B pi/toolCompleted \fR{\fB"tool_name"\fR: "...", \fB"is_error"\fR: boolean}\fR
Emitted when native tool execution finishes.

.SH NATIVE TOOLS & SAFETY GUARANTEES
\fBpi-rs\fR provides built-in tools with strict safety guarantees:
.TP
.B read
View files or line slices. 1-indexed, boundary-guarded against out-of-range slicing.
.TP
.B write
Create or overwrite files. Automatically performs atomic parent directory creation (\fBmkdir -p\fR).
.TP
.B edit
Surgical find-and-replace text edits. Requires exact single-match uniqueness (\fIoccurrences == 1\fR) to prevent unintended duplicate replacements.
.TP
.B bash
Execute shell commands asynchronously with process tree isolation and an enforced 120-second timeout. Kills zombie child handles on cancellation.
.TP
.B grep
Fast recursive regex/string search. Injects \fB\-e\fR flag to prevent command-line option injection.
.TP
.B find
Search files and directory trees by pattern.
.TP
.B ls
List directory contents with file metadata and indicators.
.TP
.B web_fetch
Fetch URLs and convert HTML content to clean Markdown using connection-pooled HTTP client with script/style stripping.
.TP
.B web_search
Live search engine queries returning organic result links and text snippets.
.TP
.B git
Execute safe parameterized Git actions (\fIstatus\fR, \fIdiff\fR, \fIlog\fR, \fIcommit\fR).
.TP
.B git_worktree
Manage isolated Git worktrees for safe parallel swarm task execution.
.TP
.B github
Inspect pull requests and issues via \fBgh\fR CLI.
.TP
.B lsp
Language server diagnostics, document symbols, definitions, and type hover.
.TP
.B ast
AST-aware structural code slicing for precise symbol extraction.
.TP
.B mcp
Universal Model Context Protocol client for stdio/HTTP external tool servers.
.TP
.B subagents
Spawn, monitor, and coordinate background subagents.

.SH NEOVIM INTEGRATION (pi.nvim)
The repository includes a native Neovim plugin in \fIlua/pi/\fR that communicates with \fBpi-rs --rpc\fR.

.SS User Commands
.TP
.B :Pi
Open or toggle the Pi interactive chat window.
.TP
.B :PiPrompt \fI[PROMPT]\fR
Send a prompt to the background \fBpi-rs\fR agent.
.TP
.B :PiModels
Open floating picker to select active LLM model.
.TP
.B :PiDiff
Display diff between buffer and agent workspace modifications.
.TP
.B :PiTree
Inspect session DAG branch history.
.TP
.B :PiStatus
Check RPC daemon health and connection state.
.TP
.B :PiStop
Cancel active agent execution turn.

.SH CONFIGURATION & FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pi/config.json
Global user configuration file storing default model, theme, telemetry preferences, and provider overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/agent/models.json
Cached model catalog containing discovered online provider and local daemon models.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/agent/auth.json
Encrypted/plaintext provider API keys and authentication tokens.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/sessions/*.jsonl
Recorded session DAG trees and conversation histories stored in append-only JSONL format.
.TP
.I AGENTS.md
Workspace-specific agent guidelines and architectural invariants loaded into system prompt context automatically.
.TP
.I skills/*/SKILL.md
Modular skill definition directories containing specialized instructions and prompt workflows.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API key for Anthropic models (Claude 3.7 Sonnet, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, Haiku).
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API key for OpenAI models (GPT-4o, o1, o3-mini).
.TP
.B GEMINI_API_KEY
API key for Google Gemini models (Gemini 2.5 Pro, Flash).
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
API key for OpenRouter meta-provider.
.TP
.B KILO_API_KEY
API key for Kilo Gateway (DeepSeek R1, V3, Qwen 2.5 Coder).
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Base URL for local Ollama server (defaults to \fIhttp://localhost:11434\fR).
.TP
.B LMSTUDIO_HOST
Base URL for LM Studio local server (defaults to \fIhttp://localhost:1234/v1\fR).
.TP
.B PI_THEME
Override default TUI color theme.

.SH MULTI-AGENT SWARM COORDINATION
\fBpi-rs\fR natively integrates with:
.TP
.B First Mate Protocol
Automated Scout/Ship branch workflows with isolated Git worktree sandboxing, automated verification suites, and atomic PR submission.
.TP
.B Herdr Swarm Protocol
Multi-agent terminal multiplexing with OSC ANSI terminal status codes, live state broadcasts (\fIidle\fR, \fIstreaming\fR, \fItool_executing\fR, \fIcompacting\fR, \fIwaiting_input\fR), and lock-free agent message channels.

